UNDERGROUND CABLE ELECTRIC FIELD PHYSICS
621.319 power cables

CABLE TYPES
  PILC   Paper-insulated lead-covered   (older)
  XLPE   Cross-linked polyethylene      (modern)
  EPR    Ethylene propylene rubber      (modern)

IDEAL COAXIAL FIELD
  E(r) = V / [ r * ln(b / a) ]

  E(r)  electric field at radius r     [V/m]
  V     applied voltage                [V]
  a     conductor outer radius         [m]
  b     insulation outer radius        [m]
  r     radial position  (a < r < b)   [m]

3-CORE APPROXIMATION
  E ≈ V / [ r * ln(D / r) ]

  D     conductor center-to-center spacing

FUNDAMENTALS
  Field peaks at the conductor surface (r = a)
  Stress falls as 1/r inside the insulation
  Dielectric: ε = ε_r ε_0
  XLPE typical ε_r ≈ 2.2 – 3.5
  Design goal: shape geometry so peak stress
               stays below insulation breakdown
